{"name":"Coastal Surf","hex":"#2d4982","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coastal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to the coast; on or near the coast; longshore."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coastal"},{"term":"surf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Waves that break on an ocean shoreline.","An instance or session of riding a surfboard in the surf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ride a wave on a surfboard; to pursue or take part in the sport of surfing.","To surf at a specified place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coast","blocks":[{"text":"A coast is the land next to the sea or the line that forms the boundary between the land and the ocean or a lake. Coasts are influenced by the topography of the surrounding landscape and by aquatic erosion, such as that caused by waves. The geological composition of rock and soil dictates the type of shore that is created. Earth has about 620,000.0 km (385,250.1 mi) of coastline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C